# The causes of the Second World War
subtitle: "How a resented peace, a toothless League and the slump made a second war possible, and why four unanswered gambles brought it in 1939."
tags: ["world history","treaty of versailles","world war ii","hitler","league of nations","great depression"]
teaches: ["history/causes-of-world-war-ii","history/treaty-of-versailles","history/appeasement-policy","concepts/historical-causation"]
thumb: "band \"Peace for our time?\" stamp \"11 MONTHS\" picture \"File:MunichAgreement.jpg\""

## The causes of the Second World War
style: documentary
use: world_map
with:
    focus:
      - Germany
      - Poland
      - Czechia
      - Austria
      - Slovakia
      - Hungary
      - Switzerland
      - Belgium
      - Netherlands
      - Luxembourg
    highlight: []
    markers:
      - {at: [13.4, 52.52], label: Berlin}
      - {at: [6.96, 50.94], label: Rhineland '36}
      - {at: [16.37, 48.21], label: Austria '38}
      - {at: [13.6, 50.65], label: Sudetenland '38}
      - {at: [14.42, 50.08], label: Prague '39}
sources:
    - id: overy
      title: The Origins of the Second World War
      authors: Richard Overy
      year: 1987
      finding: Long causes made war possible; Hitler's gambles and the failure to deter them made it come
    - id: macmillan
      title: 'Peacemakers: The Paris Conference of 1919'
      authors: Margaret MacMillan
      year: 2001
      finding: What the Versailles treaty laid down and how Germans received it
    - id: taylor
      title: The Origins of the Second World War
      authors: A. J. P. Taylor
      year: 1961
      finding: Hitler as a gambler who exploited each opening others left him

